  triage:foundIn triage:AICH-S3 ;
  triage:title "ADR-033/http-api.md/openapi.yaml route tables still drift from api.rs live routes, specifically peer-sync" ;
  triage:description "Round-3 req-qa recheck (2026-07-26) on feature/pAI-s23-crosshost-shared-write-path @ 985a6d46. Prior round-2 followup_pass (2026-07-25) marked finding as 'fixed' based on verification that ADR-033 Decision and openapi.yaml were updated to include peer-sync. Round 3 discovery: docs/atm-daemon/http-api.md was not comprehensively updated. While http-api.md Resource contract table (lines 50-62) now documents 7 resources (Write, List, Peek, Receive, Clear, Doctor, Compatibility), it still omits the two routes added in AI.23: (1) /peers/{peer}/sync and (2) /runtime/reload. ADR-033 Decision (docs/adr/ADR-033-http-endpoint-contract.md:20-34) and openapi.yaml (docs/atm-daemon/openapi.yaml:8-69) are correct and complete per round-2 fix. Actual api.rs implementation (crates/atm-core/src/api.rs endpoint_for/decode_route_request) supports 9 routes: Write, List, Peek, Receive, Clear, Doctor, CompatibilityPreflight, Heartbeat, and PeerSync. Round-2 verification was premature: only checked ADR-033 and openapi.yaml, failed to check http-api.md. Round-3 correction: http-api.md Resource table must be updated to include peer-sync and reload, cross-referencing the authoritative HTTP_ROUTE_INVENTORY constant in api.rs. Reopening as fixed_partial: ADR-033 and openapi.yaml complete, http-api.md incomplete." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "documentation" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-07-26T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:closureNote "AICH-S11-QA-BATCH-1: verified fixed on commit 82226b4c (PR #651, fix/findings-closeout). docs/adr/ADR-033-http-endpoint-contract.md now adds /runtime/reload; docs/atm-daemon/http-api.md Resource contract table adds /v1/atm/runtime/reload and removes the fictitious separate /v1/atm/message/{message-id}/ack row, replacing it with prose explaining acks route through POST /v1/atm/messages with only acknowledges_message_id populated. Cross-checked against the live crates/atm-core/src/api.rs::HTTP_ROUTE_SPECS table (10 entries: List/Write/Clear/Inspect/Receive/Doctor/PeerSync/RuntimeReload/Compatibility/Heartbeat) -- no separate ack route exists live, confirming the doc correction is accurate, not just plausible. ADR-033 and openapi.yaml were already correct from round 2. All three docs now reconciled with live routes." ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-07-26T00:55:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI23-IMPORTANT-004/fix-findings-closeout/1> ;
